From 51d57b5494f2bb2aa2622b32965046ddfce3d22c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:21:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] WIP: LocalSend stop-reading test that really stalls the
 server

The send buffer of the server's connections is capped (every answer is
short JSON); a stalled peer then pins little kernel memory and its answers
back up at once rather than after megabytes of autotuned buffer, which
also made the old test pass on header timeouts without ever stalling.
The test now takes all 32 connections, checks a 33rd is dropped, and
isolates the write deadline from the connection lifetime.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
